BT /F1 10 Tf 50 800 Td 14 TL () ' (ARTICLE 1 DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION) ' (This Facility Agreement is made between Konkan Cements Limited \(the Borrower\) and Bharat) ' (Commercial Bank Limited \(the Lender\) for a term loan facility of INR 850 crore.) ' () ' (Business Day means a day on which banks are open for general business in Mumbai. Financial) ' (Year means the period of twelve months ending on 31 March of each year.) ' () ' (EBITDA means profit before tax, interest, depreciation and amortisation, as shown in the) ' (audited consolidated financial statements of the Borrower.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 2 THE FACILITY) ' (The Borrower may request a drawdown by giving the Lender not less than 5 \(five\) Business) ' (Days notice, and each drawdown shall not be less than INR 25 crore.) ' () ' (The Borrower may prepay the facility after giving not less than 30 \(thirty\) days prior) ' (written notice to the Lender.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 7 FINANCIAL COVENANTS) ' (7.1 The Borrower shall ensure that the Debt Service Coverage Ratio shall not be less than) ' (1.35 times, tested quarterly on a trailing twelve month basis.) ' () ' (7.2 Total Debt to EBITDA shall not be more than 3.50 times on each test date.) ' () ' (7.3 The Interest Coverage Ratio shall at no time be lower than 2.25 times.) ' () ' (7.4 The Borrower shall maintain a Tangible Net Worth of not less than INR 600 Crores at all) ' (times.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 8 UNDERTAKINGS) ' (8.1 The Borrower shall not create any lien, charge or encumbrance over its assets without) ' (the prior written consent of the Lender.) ' () ' (8.2 The Borrower shall keep its plant and stocks insured against all risks and shall) ' (maintain the insurance policies in force throughout the tenor.) ' () ' () ' (ARTICLE 9 EVENTS OF DEFAULT) ' (Any amount unpaid for more than 7 \(seven\) days after its due date is an Event of Default.) ' () ' (A cure period of 30 \(thirty\) days applies to any breach of the financial covenants that is) ' (capable of remedy.) ' () ' ET
